  "chooseSection": {
    "heading": "How to Choose an Expensify Alternative",
    "body": "In our internal cost analysis, we modeled monthly software cost at three team sizes from each published per-seat price. The model assumes every member is a paid seat on a standard self-serve plan (Sage Expense Management bills annually), with no add-ons, card rewards or travel fees.\n\n- 5 members: Expensify $25, Zoho Expense $20, Ramp $0, Brex Essentials $0, BILL Spend & Expense $0, Sage Expense Management $59.95, Rydoo $60, Brex Premium $60.\n- 25 members: Expensify $125, Zoho Expense $100, Ramp $0, Brex Essentials $0, BILL Spend & Expense $0, Sage Expense Management $299.75, Rydoo $300, Brex Premium $300.\n- 100 members: Expensify $500, Zoho Expense $400, Ramp $0, Brex Essentials $0, BILL Spend & Expense $0, Sage Expense Management $1,199, Rydoo $1,200, Brex Premium $1,200.\n\nZoho Expense saves $60 a year at 5 members and $1,200 a year at 100. Ramp, Brex Essentials and BILL Spend & Expense remove the whole bill: $300, $1,500 and $6,000 a year. Rydoo, Sage Expense Management and Brex Premium cost more than double Expensify at every size.\n\nBreak-even counterexample: at 3 members Expensify Collect costs $15 a month, while Zoho Expense's Free plan, capped at 3 users, costs $0. At 4 members Expensify Collect is $20 a month, and Rydoo and Sage Expense Management both state a 5-user starting point that costs $60 and $59.95. Below 5 users Expensify beats both, and a fourth member pushes a team from Zoho Expense Free to Standard at $16 a month.\n\nOnce the totals are clear, four checks narrow the list:\n- Count paying members and compare that number with billing minimums: Rydoo starts at 5 users and Sage Expense Management bills a minimum of 5.\n- Pick monthly or annual billing, since Zoho Expense drops from $4 to $3 per user and Rydoo from $12 to $9 on annual terms.\n- Price the upgrade tier as well as the entry plan: Brex Premium is $12 per user and Ramp Plus is $15 per user plus an unpublished platform fee.\n- Treat the totals above as seat costs only, because card rewards, travel booking fees and implementation fees sit outside the model.\n\nFor the accounting software side of the same budget, our [accounting software roundup for freelancers](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) and [QuickBooks alternatives](/alternatives/quickbooks/) page list more options."
  },
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "heading": "Zoho Expense Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Zoho Expense is the closest paid match to Expensify on price, at $4 per user per month on the Standard plan billed monthly, or $3 billed annually. Its Free plan costs $0 and is capped at 3 users, so a three-person team pays no software fee.\n\nOn the modeled sizes, Zoho Expense Standard costs $20, $100 and $400 a month at 5, 25 and 100 members. That saves $60, $300 and $1,200 a year against Expensify Collect. Annual billing widens the gap: 25 members at $3 a user is $75 a month against Expensify's $125, a $600 yearly saving.\n\nZoho Expense fits teams that want a paid per-user plan priced below Expensify's $5. It costs more than Ramp Free, Brex Essentials and BILL Spend & Expense, which list $0 per user. A fourth member also moves a team off the Free plan and onto Standard at $16 a month."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Ramp Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Ramp lists two tiers: a Free plan at $0 per user per month and a Plus plan at $15 per user per month plus a platform fee based on team size. Ramp does not publish that platform fee as a number, so a full Ramp Plus total cannot be calculated from public pricing.\n\nOn the Free plan, Ramp costs $0 at 5, 25 and 100 members, which removes $300, $1,500 and $6,000 a year of Expensify Collect cost at those sizes. Ramp Free fits teams that want a $0 per-user software price with a published per-user rate for the next tier up.\n\nRamp Plus costs more than Expensify on the per-user charge alone. At 25 members, that charge is $375 a month before the platform fee, three times Expensify Collect's $125. Teams that expect to need Ramp Plus face an unknown total, while Expensify Collect keeps a lower published bill."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Brex Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Brex publishes two tiers: Essentials at $0 per user per month and Premium at $12 per user per month. Brex Essentials matches Ramp Free and BILL Spend & Expense at $0 across all three modeled team sizes.\n\nBrex Premium runs the other way. It costs $60, $300 and $1,200 a month at 5, 25 and 100 members, which is $35, $175 and $700 a month more than Expensify Collect. At 100 members, that adds up to $8,400 a year more than Expensify.\n\nBrex Essentials fits teams that want a $0 per-user plan with a published price for the paid tier. Brex Premium fits teams willing to pay $7 per user per month more than Expensify Collect. Our [Brex alternatives](/alternatives/brex/) page covers more providers priced against Brex."
    },
    {
      "heading": "BILL Spend & Expense Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "BILL Spend & Expense lists $0 per user per month, with no subscription and no per-user software fee. Its modeled cost is $0 at 5, 25 and 100 members, tied with Ramp Free and Brex Essentials for the lowest total.\n\nAgainst Expensify Collect, BILL Spend & Expense saves $25, $125 and $500 a month at the three sizes. On a yearly basis that is $300, $1,500 and $6,000. Because BILL charges no per-user fee, its published software price does not rise as a team adds members.\n\nBILL Spend & Expense fits teams that want software cost held at $0 as head count grows. The pricing facts we captured list one Spend & Expense plan and no paid tier, so there is no published upgrade price to compare against Expensify Control's starting rate of $9 per member."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Sage Expense Management Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Sage Expense Management, formerly Fyle, prices its Growth plan at $11.99 per active user per month billed annually, with minimum billing of 5 users. No monthly-billing rate appears in the pricing facts we captured.\n\nAt 5, 25 and 100 members, the Growth plan costs $59.95, $299.75 and $1,199 a month, or $719.40, $3,597 and $14,388 a year. Against Expensify Collect, that is $419.40, $2,097 and $8,388 a year more.\n\nThe 5-user minimum hits small teams hardest: a 2-person team is billed for 5 users, or $59.95 a month, against $10 on Expensify Collect. Sage Expense Management fits teams of 5 or more that accept annual billing and want per-active-user pricing. It costs more than Expensify at every modeled size."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Rydoo Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Rydoo's Essentials plan costs $12 per user per month billed monthly or $9 billed annually, and Rydoo states a 5-user starting point. On monthly billing, Rydoo Essentials costs $60, $300 and $1,200 a month at 5, 25 and 100 members.\n\nAnnual billing lowers that to $45, $225 and $900 a month. Those totals are still $20, $100 and $400 a month above Expensify Collect at the same sizes, or $4,800 a year at 100 members.\n\nRydoo's $12 monthly rate ties Brex Premium, sits one cent above Sage Expense Management and sits $3 below Ramp Plus before Ramp's platform fee. On annual terms, Rydoo's $9 undercuts Sage Expense Management's $11.99 by $2.99 per user. Rydoo fits teams of 5 or more choosing it for reasons outside this price model, since it costs more than Expensify at every modeled size."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Who This Is Not For",
      "body": "This comparison does not fit buyers whose choice depends on corporate card rewards, travel booking fees, implementation costs or negotiated enterprise discounts, because the model excludes all four. Those buyers need a written quote from each provider before the totals here apply. The model also stops at Expensify Control's listed starting price of $9 per member per month, so teams on custom Control pricing fall outside these numbers.\n\nSolo freelancers who log only their own expenses can start with our [expense report template](/templates/expense-report-template/) before paying for any seat. A team of 3 or fewer has two $0 software paths in this table besides the three $0 plans: Zoho Expense Free and Expensify Submit."
    },
    {
      "heading": "What Would Change Our Answer",
      "body": "Our answer changes if any of five published prices or limits move:\n- Expensify changes its $5 Collect price; a cut to $4 would tie Zoho Expense Standard billed monthly.\n- Zoho Expense changes its $4 Standard price or raises its Free plan above 3 users.\n- Ramp, Brex or BILL adds a per-user fee to its $0 plan, which would shrink the $6,000 yearly saving at 100 members.\n- Ramp publishes its Plus platform fee, which would let us price Ramp Plus in full.\n- Rydoo or Sage Expense Management drops its 5-user starting point or prices below $5 per user, which would reopen the small-team math.\n\nEach of these would change the scenario totals in the table above, and a price cut by Rydoo, Sage Expense Management or Brex Premium to below $5 would move that provider ahead of Expensify Collect."
    }
  ],
  "stillBetterFit": {
    "heading": "When Expensify Is Still the Better Fit",
    "body": "Expensify Collect costs less than Rydoo, Sage Expense Management and Brex Premium at every modeled team size. At 25 members, Expensify Collect is $125 a month against $300 for Rydoo Essentials billed monthly, $299.75 for Sage Expense Management and $300 for Brex Premium.\n\nTeams below 5 members are the clearest case. At 4 members, Expensify Collect is $20 a month, while Rydoo and Sage Expense Management both state a 5-user starting point that puts them at $60 and $59.95. Expensify also lists a free Submit plan alongside Collect.\n\nExpensify beats Ramp Plus on published per-user price, $5 against $15 before Ramp's unpublished platform fee. Zoho Expense Standard is the only paid tier in this comparison priced below Expensify Collect. If you already use Expensify and your team needs a paid tier, every paid alternative here except Zoho Expense Standard carries a higher per-user bill."
  },
  "verdict": "Ramp Free, Brex Essentials and BILL Spend & Expense list $0 per user, saving $6,000 a year against Expensify Collect at 100 members in our cost model. Zoho Expense fits teams that want a paid plan under $5 per user, saving $1,200 a year at 100 members on monthly billing. Expensify Collect is the better fit against Rydoo, Sage Expense Management and Brex Premium, which cost more than double at every modeled size, and for teams under 5 members facing those 5-user starting points. Count the members who submit expenses each month, multiply by each rate in the comparison table, and shortlist the two lowest-cost Expensify alternatives at that head count.",
